1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.655
Welcome to Day 1.

2
00:00:03.705 --> 00:00:09.571
When everyday movements start
feeling harder on your knees,

3
00:00:09.621 --> 00:00:13.783
it's worth looking beyond the knee itself.

4
00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:18.596
Your hips and leg muscles
also play an important

5
00:00:18.646 --> 00:00:22.407
role in how you stand, walk, and move.

6
00:00:22.457 --> 00:00:27.320
Today, we'll introduce
three gentle strengthening

7
00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:32.334
movements to help you begin
building that support.

8
00:00:32.384 --> 00:00:37.950
Go at your own pace, and feel
free to pause at any time.

9
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.119
Your knee works mostly like a hinge.

10
00:00:45.169 --> 00:00:51.721
It bends and straightens as you sit
down, stand up, walk, and climb stairs.

11
00:00:51.771 --> 00:00:54.449
But it doesn't work on its own.

12
00:00:54.499 --> 00:00:58.762
Above it is your hip, and
below it is your ankle.

13
00:00:58.812 --> 00:01:05.188
How these joints move, and how well
the surrounding muscles support them,

14
00:01:05.238 --> 00:01:10.117
can influence how your knee
is guided through each step.

15
00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:14.254
Knee discomfort can have
many different causes,

16
00:01:14.304 --> 00:01:18.744
and this video can't tell
you what is behind yours.

17
00:01:18.794 --> 00:01:22.793
What we can do is gently
build strength in the

18
00:01:22.843 --> 00:01:25.962
muscles around your hips and thighs.

19
00:01:26.012 --> 00:01:30.803
Stretching has its place,
but strengthening helps those

20
00:01:30.853 --> 00:01:34.764
muscles support you
during everyday movement.

21
00:01:34.814 --> 00:01:38.549
We'll keep every movement
slow, controlled,

22
00:01:38.599 --> 00:01:42.950
and within a range that
feels comfortable for you.

23
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.430
Our first movement is the
seated knee extension.

24
00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:54.655
Choose a sturdy chair without wheels,

25
00:01:54.705 --> 00:02:00.135
ideally placed against a
wall so it can't slide.

26
00:02:00.185 --> 00:02:07.556
Sit tall toward the front of the
seat, with both feet flat on the

27
00:02:07.606 --> 00:02:13.950
floor and your hands resting
on the seat or your thighs.

28
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.021
Slowly straighten your right knee,

29
00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:24.253
lifting your foot until your leg is
as straight as feels comfortable.

30
00:02:24.303 --> 00:02:28.950
Pause briefly, then lower
it back down with control.

31
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.950
One.

32
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.950
Two.

33
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.950
Three.

34
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.950
Four.

35
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.950
Five.

36
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.700
Rest your foot on the floor.

37
00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:05.941
Now let's switch to the left leg.

38
00:03:05.991 --> 00:03:10.950
Same slow lift, brief pause,
and controlled return.

39
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.950
One.

40
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.950
Two.

41
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.950
Three.

42
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.950
Four.

43
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.950
Five.

44
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.817
Nicely done.

45
00:03:43.867 --> 00:03:48.950
Take a breath before we stand up.

46
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.477
Next is the supported
standing hip extension.

47
00:03:54.527 --> 00:04:01.820
Stand facing a sturdy counter, with
both hands resting on it for support.

48
00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:06.950
Stand tall, feet about
hip-width apart, knees soft.

49
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.880
Keeping your upper body upright,

50
00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:16.281
gently move your right leg
backward, just a short distance.

51
00:04:16.331 --> 00:04:18.570
You don't need to go far.

52
00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.950
Then slowly bring it back.

53
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.950
One.

54
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.950
Two.

55
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.950
Three.

56
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.950
Four.

57
00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.950
Five.

58
00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.006
Bring that foot back beside the other one.

59
00:04:57.056 --> 00:04:59.052
Now the left leg.

60
00:04:59.102 --> 00:05:04.950
Keep your chest lifted
and avoid leaning forward.

61
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.950
One.

62
00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.950
Two.

63
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.950
Three.

64
00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.950
Four.

65
00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.950
Five.

66
00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.715
Well done.

67
00:05:37.765 --> 00:05:47.950
If you'd like, take a short
rest before the last movement.

68
00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.682
Our final movement is the
supported sit-to-stand.

69
00:05:55.732 --> 00:06:01.414
Use the same sturdy chair,
placed against a wall.

70
00:06:01.464 --> 00:06:05.392
Move toward the front of the seat,

71
00:06:05.442 --> 00:06:12.878
feet flat and about hip-width
apart, slightly behind your knees.

72
00:06:12.928 --> 00:06:20.950
You're welcome to use your hands on
the seat or armrests for support.

73
00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:29.916
Lean your chest slightly forward, press
through your feet, and stand up tall.

74
00:06:29.966 --> 00:06:36.950
Then reach back for the chair and
lower yourself slowly to the seat.

75
00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.950
One.

76
00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.950
Two.

77
00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.950
Three.

78
00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.950
Four.

79
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.950
Five.

80
00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:24.348
If five feels like too many
today, it's fine to do fewer.

81
00:07:24.398 --> 00:07:28.950
Stop if anything feels sharp or unsteady.

82
00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.275
That's Day 1 complete.

83
00:07:33.325 --> 00:07:38.348
A few gentle, consistent
sessions are often more

84
00:07:38.398 --> 00:07:42.999
useful than trying to
do everything at once.

85
00:07:43.049 --> 00:07:51.031
Before you go, please take a moment to
complete today's check-in in the app.

86
00:07:51.081 --> 00:07:55.153
It helps shape what comes next for you.

87
00:07:55.203 --> 00:07:56.950
See you tomorrow.

